# Docker does not read .gitignore.
#
# The Dockerfile here is a single stage ending in `COPY . .`, so without this
# file everything in the folder goes into the image and stays in its layers -
# including .env, which holds the database password, JWT_SECRET, all five R2
# keys and the Gmail app password. `docker history` reads those back out of
# any copy of the image. The scratch scripts went in the same way, and so did
# a Windows node_modules, straight over the Alpine one `npm ci` had just
# installed.

# Secrets. Nothing in this family belongs in an image.
.env
.env.*

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`; the host copy is the wrong platform.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# History, logs, and anything written at runtime.
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
*.log
logs
uploads

# Generated inside the image by `npx prisma generate`.
src/generated

# Scratch, test and utility scripts. Kept in step with .gitignore - these talk
# straight to whatever DATABASE_URL points at, so they have no business
# travelling with the application.
fix-admin.js
fix_publish_all.js
fix_user_auth.js
scratch_check_users.js
test-dashboard.js
test-users.js
reset-admin-pwd.js
dump-users.js

# The build instructions themselves.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
